SECOND ROUND (2026-11-21 03:40): channel numbers, and who owns the RX buffers
================================================================================

Both were read out of the vendor module this board actually ships
(/vendor_dlkm/lib/modules/sprdbt_tty.ko, 73998 B, sha256 f586fef4...) and confirmed on the
device.

4. BT_RX_CHANNEL 2 and BT_TX_CHANNEL0 1 are PCIe-style numbers, not this board's channels.

   mchn_ops_t is 144 bytes with hif_type@0, channel@4, inout@0x4c, pool_size@0x58 (pahole on
   our own .ko). The vendor's .data then reads:

       bt_rx_ops  @0x108: hif_type 0 (SDIO), channel 17, inout 0 (RX), pool_size 1
       bt_tx_ops0 @0x198: hif_type 0 (SDIO), channel  3, inout 1 (TX), pool_size 64

   The SDIO bus numbers RX channels from SDIO_CHN_TX_NUM (12) upwards, so 17 is bus subtype
   5. With 2, sdiohal_get_rx_channel_list() computes list_rx[2 - 12] = list_rx[-10] - an
   out-of-bounds index - and the buffers handed to the card carry subtype 6 instead of 5, so
   every read returned our own zeroed buffer. Channel 14 is not usable either: WCN_ASSERT_RX
   owns it (WCN_AT_TX=0, WCN_LOOPCHECK_RX=12, WCN_AT_RX=13, WCN_ASSERT_RX=14, WCN_RING_RX=15)
   and bus_chn_init() refuses a channel that already has ops:

       WCN BUS: [+]bus_chn_init(14, 1)
       WCN BUS: bus_chn_init err, hif_type 1

   With 17/3 both registrations succeed:

       WCN BUS: [+]bus_chn_init(17, 1)
       WCN BUS: [-]bus_chn_init(17)
       WCN BUS: [+]bus_chn_init(3, 1)
       WCN BUS: [-]bus_chn_init(3)

5. The module must not allocate its own RX buffers on SDIO.

   sdiohal_init() allocates SDIOHAL_RX_NODE_NUM page-backed nodes into p_data->list_rx_buf
   and hands them up through pop_link; sdiohal_rx_list_free() returns each one with
   put_page(virt_to_head_page(buf)). Pushing dma_alloc_coherent() buffers - what
   mtty_dma_buf_alloc() did - runs that put_page on memory that never came from alloc_pages():

       pc : sdiohal_rx_list_free+0x74/0x160 [wcn_bsp]
       <  sdiohal_list_push+0x244/0x298 [wcn_bsp]
       <  mtty_dma_buf_alloc+0x138/0x198 [sprdbt_tty]
       <  mtty_open+0xbc/0x120 [sprdbt_tty]
       Internal error: Oops: 0000000096000006

   The vendor agrees: mtty_open's only calls are sitm_ini, start_marlin and prints; mtty_close's
   are stop_marlin, kfifo_free, kfree. Neither touches a buffer pool. Dropping both calls
   removes the crash; the RX buffers stay the bus's.

Still open: the controller does not answer. btattach attaches and hci0 appears, the 0xFCA0
PSKey command goes out with the right framing on channel 3, and RX arrives on channel 17, but
no HCI event comes back, so bt-init parks holding the tty (it must not close: mtty_close frees
RX mbufs still queued on the bus and sdiohal_tx_list_denq then walks that freed list and
panics). Wi-Fi on the same card is unaffected throughout (wlan0 is an 80 MHz AP on channel 36),
so the SDIO bus itself is healthy.
