THIRD ROUND (2026-11-21 05:00): registration timing, and why the block/unblock cycle hurts
================================================================================

6. The BT channels must be registered before any subsystem powers the chip.

   dmesg showed sprdbt_tty being insmodded from the initramfs at 2.8 s and failing on unknown
   symbols (wcn_bsp not loaded yet), then the modem block in extra-modules trying it after
   sipa_eth - again without wcn_bsp. sprd_wlan_combo therefore loaded on its own and drove
   start_marlin(MARLIN_WIFI), and the firmware's channel table was negotiated without BT.
   The vendor module registers at probe, not at open, for the same reason.

   Fix in the rootfs, not the driver: wifi-start loads the three modules in dependency order.

       - for m in wcn_bsp sprd_wlan_combo; do
       + for m in wcn_bsp sprdbt_tty sprd_wlan_combo; do

   Measured after a cold boot:

       [20.697] WCN SDIO: sdiohal_probe func num is 1!!!   <- wcn_bsp
       [22.373] MU300-BT chn_init rx=17 ret=0              <- sprdbt_tty
       [22.373] MU300-BT chn_init tx=3 ret=0
       [22.488] WCN SDIO: sdiohal_probe func num is 1!!!   <- sprd_wlan_combo powers the chip

   and the channel registration moved from mtty_open() into mtty_probe() in the driver.

7. Never rfkill-block the BT function before opening the tty.

   bluetooth-start did "bt_rfkill 1; sleep 1; bt_rfkill 0". The block runs
   stop_marlin(MARLIN_BLUETOOTH), which leaves the card half-initialised; the following
   start_marlin() then short-circuits on first_power_on_ready, so the BT function never comes
   up. The next HCI write times out at the SDIO layer and the firmware asserts:

       MU300-BT write chn=3 count=184 push_ret=0
       WCN SDIO: sdiohal_config_packer_chain:CMD53 write failed with code -110
       WCN SDIO: sdio adma write fail ret:-1
       WCN BASE: fw assert:WCN Assert in pseudo_atc_main.c line 971, rd_len <= PSEUDO_ATC_BUFF_SIZE

   Unblocking once is what works - rfkill_bluetooth_init() already leaves the node soft-blocked,
   so a single "echo 0 > soft" is the whole power-on:

       bluetooth_set_power: end_block: 0, ret: 0
       mtty_open power on state ret = 0!
       mtty_open device success!

   With the cycle removed there is no CMD53 timeout and no assert. bluetooth-start still needs
   that line changed.

Still open after all of the above: same framing, right channels, right registration order,
clean power-on, TX accepted (push_ret 0, no CMD53 error), and still not one RX callback on any
channel from 16 to 21. The remaining difference has to be inside wcn_bsp's SDIO handling of the
BT channels, or a BT-specific enable step the vendor wcn_bsp.ko performs and our source tree
does not have.
